2186,"# Hadith Ṣaḥīḥ

**Narrated by Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif:**

He said: ""I asked Ibn Abī Awfā (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) make a bequest?' He replied, 'No.' I asked, 'Then how was the bequest written, and how did he command the people?' He answered, 'He bequeathed the Book of Allah.'""

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīh gharīb* hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Mālik ibn Mighwal.

---

*Note: This narration is recorded by al-Tirmidhī in his Sunan, in the chapters on the explanation of the obligation of the Book of Allah. The chain of transmission passes through Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ → Abū Qaṭan ʿAmr ibn al-Haytham al-Baghdādī → Mālik ibn Mighwal → Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif → ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu).*"
2187,"Zainab bint Jahsh said:""One day the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) awoke from sleep with a flushed red face"
2188,"Abdullah [bin Mas'ud] narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""In the end of time there will come a people young in years"
2189,"Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from al-Harith, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) decreed that the debt takes precedence over the bequest, whereas you recite the bequest before the debt. Abu 'Isa said: The practice according to the generality of the scholars is that the debt is given priority over the bequest."
2190,"**Narrated by Abu Habibah al-Ta'i:**

My brother bequeathed part of his estate to me. I met Abu al-Darda' and said, ""My brother has bequeathed a portion of his wealth to me. Where do you advise me to distribute it—among the poor, the needy, or those striving in the Cause of Allah?"" He replied, ""As for me, if I were in your place, I would not overlook those striving in the Cause of Allah. I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: *'The one who manumits a slave at the time of death is like the one who gives charity only when he is satiated.'*""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a *hasan sahih* hadith."
2191,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, that 'A'ishah رضي الله عنها informed him that Barirah came seeking the assistance of 'A'ishah رضي الله Regarding the payment of her manumission contract, and she had not yet paid anything of her contract. So 'A'ishah رضي الله عنها said to her: ""Return to your family, for if they wish that I pay your manumission contract on your behalf and that your clientage (al-wala') be mine, I shall do so.""**

**Barirah mentioned that to her family, but they refused and said: ""If she wishes to seek reward on your behalf, let her do so, but the clientage (al-wala') shall be ours.""**

**She mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: ""Purchase her and set her free, for indeed the clientage (al-wala') belongs to the one who sets free.""**

**Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said: ""What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah, it is not valid for him, even if he stipulates it a hundred times.""**

**Abu 'Isa [al-Tirmidhi] said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. It has been narrated through other chains from 'A'ishah رضي الله"
