2197,Busr bin Sa'eed said:During the Fitnah(in the time) of 'Uthman bin 'Affan
2198,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Rush to do good deeds. A Fitnah will occur that is like a portion of the dark night"
2199,"Ahmad bin Mani' narrated to us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq narrated to us, Husain Al-Muktib narrated to us, from 'Amr bin Shu'aib, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

""The example of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that eats until it is full, then vomits, then returns and eats its vomit.""

Abu 'Eisa said: And in this chapter there is also a narration from Ibn 'Abbas and 'Abdullah bin 'Amr."
2200,"Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Before the Hour there shall be Fitan like a portion of the dark night. Morning will come upon a man as a believer"
2201,"Ma'qil bin Yasar narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""Worship during Al-Harj is like Hijrah to me"
2202,"Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""When the sword is imposed on my Ummah"
2203,"Udaisah bint Uhban bin Safi Al-Ghifari said:""Ali bin Abi Talib came to my father to call him to go out(to fight) with him. My father said to him: 'Indeed my beloved"
2204,"Narrated by al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥulwānī, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr and Wakīʿ narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

""While we were with the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him), he was striking the ground (with a stick), when he raised his head toward the sky and said: 'There is not one among you except that his seat in the Fire and his seat in Paradise have already been known.' Wakīʿ said: '...except that his seat in the Fire and his seat in Paradise have already been written.' They said: 'Shall we not then rely (upon this decree), O Messenger of Allāh?' He said: 'No, work, for each one is facilitated for that for which he was created.'""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."
2205,"Anas bin Malik said:""I shall narrate a Hadith to you that I heard from the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w)"
2206,"Az-Zubair bin 'Adi said:""We entered upon Anas bin Malik. We complained to him about what we were experiencing from Al-Hajjaj. So he said: 'There will not be a year"
2207,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour will not be established until 'Allah"
2208,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:"" The earth will throw out pieces of its liver(in sides): liver; gold and silver will come out like columns."" He said: ""A thief will come and say: 'For this my hands were amputated?' A murderer will come and say: 'For this I killed?' One who severed ties of kinship will come and say: 'For this I severed the ties of kinship?' Then they will leave it without taking anything from it"
2209,"Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour will not be established until the happiest of people in the world is Luka' bin Luka"
2210,"Ali bin Abi Talib narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""When my Ummah does fifteen things"
2211,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""When Al-Fai' is distributed(preferentially)"
2212,"Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""In this Ummah there shall be collapsing of the earth"
2213,"Al-Mustawrid bin Shaddad Al-Fihri reported that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""I was sent in advance of the Hour"
2214,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour and I were dispatched like these two"" - and Abu Dawud(a narrator) indicated with his index and middle fingers- so"
2215,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""The Hour shall not be established until you fight a people whose sandals are made out of hair"
2216,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""When Kisra is ruined"
2217,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Wāṣil ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Kūfī narrated to us, saying:** Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us, from al-Qāsim ibn Ḥabīb and ʿAlī ibn Nizār, from Nizār, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:

**The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:**

*""Two groups from my Ummah shall have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah.""*

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿUmar, Ibn ʿUmar, and Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj. This is a gharīb, ḥasan, ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""**

**Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us, saying:** Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, saying: Salām ibn Abī ʿAmrah narrated to us, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him.

Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ said: **""And Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us, saying:** ʿAlī ibn Nizār informed us, from Nizār, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, **a similar narration.""**

---

*Note: The Murji'ah (المرجئة) are those who deferred judgment on major sinners, and the Qadariyyah ("
2218,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour shall not be established until nearly thirty imposters"
2219,"Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Hour shall not be established until tribes of my Ummah unite with the idolaters"
2220,"Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""In Thaqif there will be a great liar and destroyer"
2221,"Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The best of people are my generation"
2222,"Imran bin Husain narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""The best of my Ummah is the generation among whom I was sent"
2223,"Simak bin Harb narrated from Jabir bin Samurah who said "" The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:'There will be twelve Amir after me.""' He said: ""Then he said something that I did not understand. So I asked the one who was next to me"
2224,"Ziyad bin Kusaib Al-'Adawi said:""I was with Abu Bakrah under the Minbar of Ibn 'Amir while he was giving a Khutbah wearing a fine garment. Abu Bilal said: 'Look at our Amir wearing clothes of wickedness!' So Abu Bakrah said: Be quiet! I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying: ""Whoever insults Allah's Sultan on the earth"
2225,"Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from his father who said:""It was said to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: 'Perhaps you should endorse your successor.' He said: 'If I appoint a successor"
2226,"# Hadith of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (رضي الله عنه) on the Occasion of the Day of the House (Yawm al-Dār)

**Narration:**

Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah al-Ḍabbī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf, that **ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān** (رضي الله عنه), on the **Day of the House** (*Yawm al-Dār*), looked down over the wall and said:

> ""I adjure you by Allah — do you know that the **Messenger of Allah** (صلى الله عليه وسلم) said:
>
> *'The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except for one of three: adultery after marriage (*zinā baʿda iḥṣān*), apostasy after Islam (*irtidād baʿd Islām*), or the taking of a life unjustly, for which one is killed.'*

By Allah, I never committed fornication (*zinā*) in the **Jāhiliyyah** (pre-Islamic period of ignorance), nor in Islam; nor did I ever apostatize since I pledged allegiance to the **Messenger of Allah** (صلى الله عليه وسلم); nor did I ever take the life which Allah has forbidden. **So on what basis are you killing me?**""

---

**Commentary of Imām Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (رحمه الله):**

Abū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: ""There are narrations on this topic from **Ibn Masʿūd** (رضي الله عنه), **ʿĀʾishah** (رضي الله عنها), and **Ibn ʿAbbās** (رضي الله عنهما).""

He further stated: **""This is a ḥasan (good) hadith.""**

He also noted: **Ḥammād ibn Salamah** narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd and **raised it** (*rafʿahu*, i.e., attributed it to the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم). However, **Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān** and others narrated this same hadith from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd but **stopped it** (*awqafūhu*) at the level of the Companion's statement and did not raise it.

He concluded: ""This hadith has been narrated through **multiple chains** from ʿUthmān (رضي الله عنه) from the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم) as a **marfūʿ** (elevated) narration.""

---

## Scholarly Notes:

- **Yawm al-Dār** refers to the tragic day in which ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (رضي الله عنه), the third Rightly Guided Caliph (*Khalīfah al-Rāshid*), was besieged in his home and ultimately martyred in 35 AH (656 CE).
- The hadith establishes the **fundamental Islamic principle** that the sanctity of Muslim blood is inviolable, and capital punishment is restricted exclusively to three categories, as established by the Prophet (صلى الله عليه وسلم).
- ʿUthmān (رضي الله عنه) invoked this hadith as a **legal and moral defense** against the charges laid by the rebels who besieged him, demonstrating his profound knowledge of the Sunnah and his unwavering adherence to Islamic conduct throughout his life.
- The discussion of **rafʿ** (elevation to the Prophet صلى الله عليه"
2227,"Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhail said:"" There were some people from(the tribe of) Rabiah with 'Amr bin Al-'As"
2228,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The night and the day shall not go away until a man called Jahjah among the Mawali reigns"
2229,"Thawban narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""I only fear for my Ummah from the misguiding A'immah."" He said that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: ""There will never cease to be a group from my Ummah manifest upon the truth"
2230,"Abdullah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The world shall not pass away until a man from the people of my family rules the Arabs whose name agrees with my name"
2231,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn Mu'āwiyah al-Jumaḥī al-Baṣrī**, who narrated from **Ḥammād ibn Salamah**, from **Abū al-Zubayr**, from **Jābir** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

> **The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade that a sword be handed over while drawn (unsheathed).**

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *""In this chapter (there is also a narration) from Abū Bakrah (may Allāh be pleased with him).""*

He further said: *""This is a **ḥasan gharīb** ḥadīth from the narration of Ḥammād ibn Salamah.""*

He added: *""Ibn Lahī'ah also narrated this ḥadīth from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from Bint al-Juhniyy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). However, the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Salamah is, in my view, more authentic (aṣaḥḥ).""*

---

### Scholarly Notes:

- **"
2232,"Zaid bin Al-'Ammi said:""I heard Abu As-Siddiq An-Naji narrate a Hadith from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri who said: 'We feared events to occur after our Prophet"
2233,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Ibn Mariam shall soon descend among you"
2234,"Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w): 'There was never a Prophet after Nuh but that he warned his people about the Dajjal"
2235,"Az-Zuhri narrated from Salim from Ibn 'Umar who said:""The Messengers of Allah(s.a.w)stood among the people"
2236,"Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""You shall fight the Jews. You will gain such control over them"
2237,"Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said:""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) narrated to us"
2238,"Qutaybah narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr, from ʿAbd Allāh — who is Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī al-Ashhalī — from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān (may Allāh be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour shall not come until you kill your leader (imām), fight among yourselves with your swords, and the worst among you inherit your worldly possessions.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan hadīth. We only know it from the narration of ʿAmr ibn Abī ʿAmr."
2239,"Anas bin Malik said:""Constantinople will be conquered with the coming of the Hour"
2240,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Bundār, who narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, who narrated from Sufyān, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Ṭāriq ibn Shihāb, who said:**

""The first person to deliver the sermon (*khutbah*) before the prayer was Marwān. A man stood up and said to Marwān, 'You have opposed the Sunnah.' Marwān replied, 'O so-and-so, that which was [previously observed] has been abandoned.'""

**Abū Saʿīd (may Allāh be pleased with him) said:** ""As for this man, he has fulfilled what was incumbent upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) say:

**'Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand; and if he is not able to do so, then with his tongue; and if he is not able to do so, then with his heart — and that is the weakest of faith.'**""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith.""

---

*This hadith is recorded in Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim and is among the most significant narrations concerning the obligation of enjoining good and forbidding evil (al-amr bi-l-maʿrūf wa-l-nahy ʿan al-munkar), establishing a three-tiered hierarchy of rectifying wrongdoing according to one's capacity.*"
2241,Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) was asked about the Dajjal
2242,"Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The Dajjal will come to Al-Madinah to find the angels have surrounded it. Neither the plague nor the Dajjal will enter it"
2243,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Faith is Yemeni"
2244,"Mujammi' bin Jariyah Al-Ansari said:""I heard the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) saying: 'Eisa bin Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd"
2245,"It was narrated that Anas said:""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'There was no Prophet except that he warned his Ummah of the liar who is blind in one eye. Lo! He is blind in one eye"
2246,"Abu Sa'eed said:""I was accompanied by Ibn Sa'eed- either performing Hajj or 'Umrah - the people departed"
2247,"It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed said:""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) met Ibn Sa'eed on one of the streets of Al-Madinah"
2248,"It was narrated from 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakrah from his father who said:""The Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said: 'The father of the Dajjal and hid mother"
2249,"Narrated Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ, who narrated from his father, from al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl, from Abū Naḍrah al-ʿAbdī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī رضي الله عنه, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour shall not be established until wild beasts speak to humans, until the tip of a man’s whip and the strap of his sandal speak to him, and until his thigh informs him of what his family has done after him.""

Abū ʿĪsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: There are narrations on this authority from Abū Hurayrah رضي الله عنه. This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith; we do not know it except through the narration of al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl. Al-Qāsim ibn al-Faḍl is trustworthy (*thiqah*) and reliable (*maʾmūn*) among the scholars of hadith, and he was declared trustworthy by Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī."
2250,"Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from al-Aʿmash, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said:

""The moon was split during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Bear witness (to this).'""

Abū ʿĪsā said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Ibn Masʿūd, Anas, and Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim. This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."
2251,"# Hadith of the Ten Signs of the Hour

## Text

Narrated by Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd (may Allāh be pleased with him):

He said: ""The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) appeared upon us from a chamber while we were discussing the Hour (as-Sāʿah). The Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said:

**'The Hour shall not commence until you witness ten signs: the rising of the sun from its place of setting, the emergence of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj (Gog and Magog), the emergence of the Dābbah (the Beast), three land-swallowings (khusūf): a land-swallowing in the East, a land-swallowing in the West, and a land-swallowing in the Arabian Peninsula, and a fire that emerges from the depths of ʿAden (in Yemen) that drives the people or gathers the people, and it shall pass the night with them wherever they pass the night, and it shall take its midday rest with them wherever they take their midday rest.'**

---

## Additional Narrations

**Chain of Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān → Wakīʿ → Sufyān → Furāt:**

A similar narration, with the addition of **""ad-Dukhān"" (the Smoke)**.

**Chain of Hunnād → Abū al-Aḥwaṣ → Furāt al-Qazzāz:**

A similar narration to that of Wakīʿ from Sufyān.

**Chain of Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān → Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī → Shuʿbah and al-Masʿūdī, both from Furāt al-Qazzāz:**

A similar narration to that of ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān from Sufyān from Furāt, with the addition of **""ad-Dajjāl (the False Christ) or the Smoke.""**

**Chain of Abū Mūsā (Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā) → Abū an-Nuʿmān al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbdillāh al-ʿIjlī → Shuʿbah → Furāt:**

A similar narration to that of Abū Dāwūd from Shuʿbah, with the addition that he said:

**'And the tenth sign is either a wind that casts them into the sea, or the descent of ʿĪsā (Jesus), son of Maryam (ʿalayhimā as-salām).'**

---

## Scholarly Notes

Abū ʿĪsā (at-Tirmidhī, raḥimahullāh) stated: ""And in this chapter (there are also narrations) from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), Umm Salamah (may Allāh be pleased with her), and Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy (may Allāh be pleased with her).""

**Abū ʿĪsā declared this ḥadīth to be: Ḥasan Ṣaḥīḥ (Good and Authentic).**

---

*This ḥadīth is recorded in the Sunan of at-Tirmidhī and constitutes one of the foundational narrations regarding the Major Signs of the Last Hour, including the emergence of the Dajjāl, the descent of ʿĪsā ibn Maryam (ʿalayhimā as-salām), the emergence of the Dābbah, the release of Yaʾjūj and Maʾjūj, the rising of the sun from the West, the Smoke (ad-Dukhān), three major land-swallowings, and the fire from Yemen that will drive humanity to their place of gathering (al-Mashʿar).*"
2252,"It was narrated from Ubayy bin Ka'b that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Do not curse the wind. When you see what you dislike"
2253,Fatimah bint Qais narrated that Allah's Prophet(s.a.w) ascended the Minbar
2254,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us:** Abū Mu'āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrāhīm al-Taymī, from his father, from Abū Dharr (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:

""I entered the mosque when the sun had set, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allāh be upon him) was sitting. He said: **'O Abū Dharr, do you know where this (the sun) goes?'** I said: **'Allāh and His Messenger know best.'** He said: **'Indeed, it goes and seeks permission to prostrate (in worship), and permission is granted to it. It is as though it is said to it: ""Rise from whence you came,"" and so it rises from its place of setting (i.e., the west).'**

He (the narrator) then recited: **'And that is its resting place'** (Sūrah Yāsīn, 36:38). He said: **'And that was the recitation of 'Abdullāh ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him).'**

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **'In this chapter (there are narrations) from Ṣafwān ibn 'Assāl, Ḥudhayfah ibn Asīd, Anas, and Abū Mūsā (may Allāh be pleased with them all).'**

**And this is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.**

---

*Note: This hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and is also found in Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī and Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim. It describes the sun's prostration beneath the Throne ('Arsh) of Allāh, as referenced in the Qur'ānic verse: ""And the sun runs [on course] toward its stopping point. That is the determination of the Exalted in Might, the Knowing"" (Sūrah Yāsīn, 36:38).*"
2255,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Zainab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her):**

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) awoke from sleep with his face flushed red, and he was saying: *""Lā ilāha illallāh""* (There is no god but Allah), repeating it three times. He then said: **""Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn close! Today, a breach has been made in the barrier of Ya'jūj and Ma'jūj (Gog and Magog) like this""** — and he made a circle by joining his thumb and index finger, forming a ring of ten.

Zainab (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I asked, **""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we be destroyed even though there are righteous people among us?""** He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: **""Yes, when wickedness (al-khabath) becomes abundant.""**

---

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhī, may Allah have mercy on him) said:** This is a *hasan sahīh* (good and authentic) hadith. And Sufyān (ibn 'Uyaynah) narrated this hadith with excellence (*jawwada*).

Al-Humaydī, 'Alī ibn al-Madīnī, and other Huffāz (master hadith scholars) narrated from Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah similarly to this.

Al-Humaydī said: Sufyān ibn 'Uyaynah said: **""I preserved from al-Zuhrī in this hadith the names of four women: Zainab bint Abī Salamah, from Habībah — and both were the stepdaughters of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — from Umm Habībah, from Zainab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).""**

Ma'mar and others narrated this hadith from al-Zuhrī but did not mention Habībah in the chain. Some of the companions of Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated this hadith from Ibn 'Uyaynah and did not mention Umm Habībah in it."
2256,"Abū Kurayb, Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim, from Zirr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""There will emerge at the end of time a people who are young in age and foolish in understanding. They will recite the Qurʾān, but it will not pass beyond their throats. They will speak the words of the best of creation, yet they will exit from the religion as an arrow exits the game animal.""

Abū ʿĪsā said: In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿAlī, Abū Saʿīd, and Abū Dharr. This hadith is ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ.

It has been narrated in other hadiths from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, where he described these people who recite the Qurʾān but it does not pass beyond their throats, and who exit from the religion as an arrow exits the game animal — they are the Khawārij, the Ḥarūriyyah, and others among the Khawārij."
2257,Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated from his father
2258,"Abu Wa'il narrated from Hudhaifah that 'Umar said:""Which of you remembers what the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said about the Fitnah?"" So Hudhaifah said: ""I do."" Hudhaifah said: ""A man's Fitnah is in his family"
2259,
2260,"Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""There shall come upon the people a time in which the one who is patient upon his religion will be like the one holding onto a burning ember"
2261,"Narrated by Abu Hafs, Amr ibn Ali, who narrated from Yahya ibn Said, who narrated from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, who narrated from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not revert to disbelief after me by striking the necks of one another."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Jarir, Ibn Umar, Kurz ibn Alqamah, Wathilah ibn al-Asqa', and al-Sunabihi. This Hadith is Hasan Sahih."
2262,"Abu Bakrah said:""Allah restrained me with something that I heard from the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w). When Kisra was destroyed"
2263,Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) came across some people who were sitting
2264,"Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""Shall I not inform you of the best of your leaders and the worst of them: The best of them are those whom you love and they love you"
2265,"Umm Salamah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""Indeed there shall come upon you A'immah whom you like (what they do) and some (of what they do) you dislike. So whoever rejects"
2266,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""When your leaders are the best of you"
2267,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Prophet(s.a.w) said:""You are in a time when whoever abandons a tenth of what he has been ordered"
2268,"Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) stood on the Minbar and said:""The land of Fitan is there"" and he pointed to the east"
2269,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""Black standards will come from Khurasan"
2270,"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""When time draws near"
2271,"Ubadah bin As-Samit narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""The dreams of the believer are a portion of the forty-six portions of Prophet-hood"
2272,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: 'Indeed Messenger-ship and Prophethood have been terminated"
2273,Ata' bin Yasar narrated from a man among the inhabitants of Egypt who said:I asked Abu Ad-Darda about the saying of Allah
2274,"Abu Sa'eed narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""The most truthful of dreams are in the last hours of the night"
2275,"Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Hour shall not come until it is no longer said upon the earth: 'Allah, Allah.'""

Abu Isa (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is a Hasan (good) Hadith.

It was also narrated by Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Humaid, from Anas, with a similar narration, but he did not raise it (i.e., he did not attribute it to the Prophet). And this (the Mawquf version) is more authentic than the first Hadith (the Marfu' version)."
2276,"Abdullah narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""Whoever saw me (in a dream) while sleeping then he has indeed seen me. For indeed the Shaitan can not resemble me"
2277,"Abu Qatadah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Dreams are from Allah and Hulum are from Shaitan. So when one of you sees something that bothers him"
2278,"Waki' bin 'Udus narrated that Abu Razin Al-'Uqaili said:"" The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said: "" The believer's dreams are a portion of the forty portions of Prophet-hood. And it is (as if it is) on the leg of a bird"
2279,"Waki' bin 'Udus narrated from Abu Razin that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:"" The Muslim's dreams are a portion of the forty-six portions of Prophet-hood. And it is (as if it is) on the leg of a bird"
2280,"Abu Hurarirah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Dreams are of three types: The true dream"
2281,"Abu 'Abdur-Rahman(As-Sulami) narrated from 'Ali and I think he said:"" From the Prophet(s.a.w)"
2282,(another chain) from Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami who narrated from 'Ali from the Prophet with similar narrations. [He said:This narration is Hasan.] There are narration on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas
2283,"Ibn 'Abbas narrated that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""Whoever lies about having a dream"
2284,"Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""While I was sleeping"
2285,"Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated from some of the companions of the Prophet (s.a.w) that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:""While I was sleeping I saw people presented before me"
2286,Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrated from Abu Sa'eed al-Khudri that the Prophet (s.a.w) said:similar in meaning (to no)
2287,"Abu Bakrah narrated:""One day the Prophet (s.a.w) said: ""'Who among you had a dream?' A man said: ""I did. I saw as if a scale had descended from the Heavens in which you and Abu Bakr were weighed So you outweighed Abu Bakr. Abu Bkar and 'Umar were weighed"
2288,"Aishah said:""The Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) was asked about Waraqah. Khadijah said to him: 'He believed in you"
2289,Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar about the dream of the Prophet (s.a.w) and Abu Bakr and 'Umar
2290,"Salim bin 'Abdullah narrated from his father about the dream of the Prophet (s.a.w) who said:""I saw a black woman with unkempt hair going out of Al-Madinah"
2291,"Abu Hurrairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""In the end of time"
2292,"Ibn 'abbas narrated fro Abu Hurairah that the Messengr of Allah (s.a.w) said:""I had a dream while sleeping as if there were two gold bracelets in my hands which bothered me very much. So it was reveled to me to blow them off. I blew them off and they flew away. I interpreted thwm to be two liars who would appear after me. One of them caled Masalamah of Yamamah"
2293,"Abu Hurairah narrated that a man came to the Prophet (s.a.w) and said:""I had a dream of a cloud with shade dripping butter and honey. I saw the people scooping it up with their hands"
2294,"Samurah bin Jundub narrated :""When the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) had led us in Subh(Fajr prayer)"
2295,"Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:""Shall l not inform you of the best of witnesses? The one who comes with his testimony before being asked for it"
2296,"Muhammad ibn Bashshar al-Abdiyy narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafiyy narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Umar ibn al-Hakam, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The night and the day shall not pass until a man from the freedmen (mawali) shall rule, whose name shall be Jahjah."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan gharib hadith."
2297,"Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani narrated that the Messenger of Allah(s.a.w) said:""The best of witnesses is the one who gives his testimony before being asked for it"
2298,Aishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (s.a.w) said:The testimony of a treacherous man is not acceptable nor a treacherous woman nor a man lashed for the Hadd nor a woman lashed nor one possessing malice of enmity nor a rehearsed witness nor the Qani of (one contracted by)the family on their behalf nor the one associating himself to other than his Wala or to other than his relatives
